        "date": "2026-11-07T23:57:57Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): read the cross-drill holder along its own footprint on box stock\n\ncross_holder compared the holder against the stock's corner\n(circumscribed) radius in its Z band on every move, so a box-stock\ncross drill whose holder cleared the face but not the corner circle\nwas refused. A move on one station - pose along an XY axis, sliding\nalong its hole line, across it, or in Z - now reads the material in\nthe rectangular tube its holder sweeps (cross_entry's tube clipping,\ngeneralised to a Tube with separate across and Z half-widths;\ntube_reach reads a flat at its face and a turned round at its\ncircumscribed reading, as entry does). The corner-radius band\nreading stays for swings round the bar (quarter-turn station\nchanges) and off-axis poses. Part and stock both count as material.\n\nPins: drilling_cross_holder (box clears face, generates and posts;\nmaterial in the holder's footprint still refused by name) and\ndrill_reach unit tests (on-station face reading; a swing keeps the\ncorner radius).\n\nFixes #119\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
